==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*peh₂-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|penetracioun}}, from {{der|en|fro|penetracïon}}, and its source, {{der|en|la|penetrātiō}}, from the participle stem of {{m|la|penetrō|t=pierce|pos=verb}}.  Morphologically {{suffix|en|penetrate|ion}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/pɛ.nɪˈtɹeɪ.ʃən/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/pɛ.nəˈtɹeɪ.ʃən/|a=GA}}
* {{rhymes|en|eɪʃən|s=4}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-penetration.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|eɪʃən|s=4}}
* {{hyph|en|pen|e|tra|tion}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# The act of [[penetrate|penetrating]] something. {{defdate|from 15th c.}}
# The [[insertion]] of the [[penis]] (or similar object) during [[sexual intercourse]]. {{defdate|from 17th c.}}
#: {{ux|en|Any '''penetration''', however slight, is sufficient to complete the offense.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2003|author=Parliament of the United Kingdom|title=w:Sexual Offences Act 2003|chapter=Part I, section 1(1)|url=[s:Sexual Offences Act 2003/Part 1#1.1{{!}}Wikisource]|page=1|text=A person (A) commits [[rape|an offence]] if—<br>(a) he intentionally [[penetrate]]s the vagina, anus or mouth of another person (B) with his penis,<br>(b) B does not consent to the '''penetration''', and<br>(c) A does not reasonably believe that B consents.}}
# The act of penetrating a given situation with the [[mind]] or faculties; [[perception]], [[discernment]]. {{defdate|from 17th c.}}
#* {{RQ:Scott Rob Roy|volume=II|page=46|text={{...}} my observations of her looks and actions became acutely sharpened, and that to a degree, which, notwithstanding my efforts to conceal it, could not escape her '''penetration'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1859|author=w:Henry David Thoreau|title=w:A Plea for Captain John Brown|url=https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/2567/pg2567-images.html
|passage=I have no respect for the '''penetration''' of any man who can read the report of that conversation, and still call the principal in it insane.}}
# The act of progressing or moving forward through or into something.
# {{lb|en|blackjack}} A number or fraction that represents how many cards/decks will be dealt before shuffling, in contrast to the total number of cards/decks in play.
# {{lb|en|marketing}} The [[proportion]] of the [[target]] [[audience]] who buy or use the specified product or service.

